//   2026-07-10.1 · Workbook: right-click a floating widget (chart / KPI / table / text / filter / insights tile) to get its own Edit · Duplicate · Delete menu instead of the browser's native context menu. Mirrors the header action buttons, reuses the shared cell-menu styling, and is edit-gated (read-only viewers keep the native menu). workbook.js only.
//   2026-07-10.2 · Workbook: drag-select now edge-auto-scrolls. Dragging a cell selection, a fill-handle, a column/row-header selection, or a cell move toward (or past) an edge of the grid keeps the sheet scrolling in that direction — and, crucially, keeps scrolling while the cursor is held still at the edge (the loop runs on requestAnimationFrame, not off mousemove), so you can extend a selection well beyond what's on screen without inching the mouse. Speed ramps with proximity to the edge. Supersedes the old mousemove-only nudge on cell moves. workbook.js only.
